"Passing the Brass Lantern" by Bernd Eickhoff

uses chapters/01_talos

player "They say Medea is a sorceress.\n
        They say she wields power to deceive.\n
        They are wrong.\n
        Socrates is my father, who lent me his inquisitive mind\n
        and Ulysses my mother, a wanderer and a teller of tales.\n
        I speak no lies, but the questions that shake us.\n
        This story is my undoing of Talos and the creation of the new mind in its stead."


verb talk
    takes creature noun
    "There is no one here who will answer."

kind burning: dark, lit

object Brass Lantern, lamp "The lantern is {self burning}"
    instead of examine:
        if self is lit:
            say "The lantern burns with a steady flame."
        else:
            say "The lantern is dark."

kind scene: talos, emily

object State "tracks global state"

    
